<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="yes"?><rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><channel><title>Layers on Typophile Archive</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/layers/</link><description>Recent content in Layers on Typophile Archive</description><generator>Hugo</generator><language>en-us</language><lastBuildDate>Thu, 06 Feb 2014 04:36:00 +0100</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/tags/layers/index.xml" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><title>Lichtspiele — A Typocalypse Typeface</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/113960/</link><pubDate>Thu, 06 Feb 2014 04:36:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/113960/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Lichtspiele — A typocalypse display typeface&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Cinemas from the early 20th Century are called &amp;ldquo;Lichtspiele&amp;rdquo; in Germany. &amp;ldquo;Lichtspiele&amp;rdquo; transports you back to a time where neon lights and marquee letters decorated cinema facades.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Of the 5 styles, three have two versions of italics - one for each perspective. Display is your basic style. Neon is inspired by the old neon letters found outside cinemas.&lt;br&gt;
Add Neon Outline to Display or Neon to add another layer to your artwork. Neon 3D is a extruded version of Neon. Screen Credits is based on the liner notes of movie posters.&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>New Release Yapa 50% OFF</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/107911/</link><pubDate>Mon, 30 Dec 2013 10:45:00 +0100</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/107911/</guid><description>&lt;h2 id="hello-typophiles"&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Hello Typophiles!&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
