&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src="http://web.archive.org/web/20131013020204im_/http:/typophile.com/files/font_3525.jpg" alt=""&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description></item><item><title>Slab Happy - a layered typographic system</title><link>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/102847/</link><pubDate>Tue, 07 May 2013 20:33:00 +0200</pubDate><guid>http://typophile-archive.simon-cozens.org/102847/</guid><description>&lt;p&gt;Inspired by neutral slab serifs with an added twist, Slab Happy is a typographic system consisting of eight layerable fonts with infinite combinations. Slab Happy looks best when set in display sizes, but functions just as well at smaller point sizes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The complete Slab Happy family consists of: Regular, Bold, Outline, 3D, Stitches, Fill, Shadow, and Crosshatch.&lt;/p&gt;
